class:: PartialClusterOsc
summary:: Spectrally shaped additive oscillator with unison voices
categories:: UGens>Generators>Deterministic
related:: Guides/NovelOscillators

description::

PartialClusterOsc creates a large additive spectrum whose partial spacing,
frequency warp, amplitude tilt, periodic attenuation, phase distribution, and
unison detuning can move continuously.

For zero-based partial index code::n::, the ratio is
code::(1 + (n * spacing)) ** (2 ** warp)::. A smooth activation edge follows
code::partials::, a raised-cosine mask implements spectral combing, and
components fade out before Nyquist. The active absolute-amplitude sum
normalizes each voice.

The closest vanilla UGen is link::Classes/Klang::. Both sum many sinusoidal
components, but PartialClusterOsc generates the spectrum procedurally at audio
rate, culls it against Nyquist, and includes deterministic unison and stereo
distribution.

classmethods::

method:: ar

argument:: freq
Signed fundamental frequency in hertz.

argument:: partials
Continuous active-partial count from zero through code::maxPartials::.

argument:: spacing
Positive linear distance before warping. code::1:: is harmonic when
code::warp:: is zero.

argument:: warp
Exponent control. code::0:: is neutral; negative values compress and positive
values expand upper ratios.

argument:: tilt
Power-law spectral slope. Larger values reduce upper partials.

argument:: combPeriod
Period of the smooth attenuation pattern in partial indices.

argument:: combDepth
Attenuation strength from code::0:: through code::1::. Zero is transparent.

argument:: voices
Initialization-rate unison count from code::1:: through code::5::.

argument:: detune
Maximum symmetric unison detuning in semitones.

argument:: phaseSpread
Deterministic partial-phase dispersion from code::0:: through code::1::.

argument:: maxPartials
Initialization-rate computation limit from code::1:: through code::4096::.

argument:: mul
Multiplier applied to both outputs.

argument:: add
Offset added to both outputs after multiplication.

returns::
A stereo array.

method:: kr

PartialClusterOsc is audio-rate only. This method throws an error.

subsection:: Discussion

High code::partials:: and code::voices:: values are intentionally expensive:
work and private memory scale with the product of code::maxPartials:: and
code::voices::. Scalar and control-rate shaping uses block-cooked weights and
recursive complex oscillators. If any shaping input is audio rate, the UGen
switches at construction to an exact per-sample path, which is substantially
more expensive and does not allocate the recursive bank. Extreme legal
settings are normalized and finite, but a limiter is still useful when
combining several instances.

examples::

code::
(
{ PartialClusterOsc.ar(55, 96, tilt: 1.2) * 0.045 }.play;
)
::

code::
(
{
    PartialClusterOsc.ar(
        38, partials: 240,
        warp: LFNoise1.kr(0.1).range(-0.15, 0.18),
        tilt: 1.3,
        combPeriod: LFNoise1.kr(0.07).range(2, 13),
        combDepth: LFTri.kr(0.05).range(0, 0.9),
        voices: 5, detune: 0.12,
        phaseSpread: 0.7, maxPartials: 320
    ) * 0.028
}.play;
)
::

